{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Who goes out before them.</b> Not in the manner of the kings of the nations, who sit in their houses and send their armies to war — but as I did, for I fought against Sihon and Og, as it says (Numbers 21) ״Do not fear him,״ and as Joshua did, as it says ״And Joshua went to him and said to him, Are you for us?״ etc. (Joshua 5), and likewise of David it says (I Samuel 18) ״For he goes out and comes in before them״ — goes out at the head and comes in at the head (Sifrei)." "<b>And who brings them out.</b> Through his merits." "<b>And who brings them in.</b> Through his merits. Another interpretation — <b>And who brings them in</b>: that you should not do to him as you are doing to me, for I am not bringing them into the land (Yalkut Shimoni)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:03.705616537Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}